  "term": "sense of equilibrium",
  "definition": "The sense of equilibrium is the bodily awareness involved in keeping oneself upright and balanced. It appears to depend on combined input from muscle, skin, pressure, and vision, with the ear’s semicircular canals helping maintain the muscular tone that supports balance.",
